---
import type { ChapterSummary } from "../../lib/content";

interface Props { chapters: ChapterSummary[]; authOrigin: string; contentApiOrigin: string; }
const { chapters, authOrigin, contentApiOrigin } = Astro.props;
const active = chapters.find((chapter) => chapter.order === 7) ?? chapters[0];
---

<main id="main-content" class="textbook-editor" data-editor-root data-auth-origin={authOrigin} data-content-api-origin={contentApiOrigin}>
  <header class="editor-topbar">
    <button class="product-mark" type="button" aria-label="AI Ethics Textbook home"><span aria-hidden="true">▯</span> AI Ethics Textbook</button>
    <label class="chapter-picker"><span class="visually-hidden">Current chapter</span><select data-chapter aria-describedby="chapter-canary-note">{chapters.map((chapter) => <option value={`chapter_ch${String(chapter.order).padStart(2, "0")}`} selected={chapter.slug === active.slug} data-order={chapter.order} data-title={chapter.title} data-editable={chapter.order === 7 ? "true" : "false"}>{chapter.order}. {chapter.title} — {chapter.order === 7 ? "editable canary" : "read-only until cutover"}</option>)}</select><small id="chapter-canary-note">Browse all 18 chapters here. Chapter 7 is the writable canary; each later chapter unlocks only after its controlled D1 cutover.</small></label>
    <button class="release-state" type="button" data-release-state><i></i> Draft <span aria-hidden="true">⌄</span></button>
    <div class="top-actions"><button type="button" data-preview aria-label="Preview chapter">◉ <span>Preview</span></button><button type="button" data-review aria-label="Review changes">▢ <span>Review changes</span><b data-change-count>0</b></button><button type="button" data-validate aria-label="Validate change set">✓ <span>Validate</span></button><button class="publish" type="button" data-submit-review aria-label="Submit change set for review">⇧ <span>Submit review</span></button><button type="button" data-login hidden>Sign in with GitHub</button><button type="button" data-logout hidden>Sign out</button><button class="more" type="button" data-publish aria-label="Publication status">⋮</button></div>
  </header>

  <div class="editor-workspace">
    <nav class="editor-nav" aria-label="Editor workspace">
      <button class="mobile-nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="editor-navigation-items">☰ <span>Menu</span></button>
      <div class="nav-items" id="editor-navigation-items" data-nav-items>
        <button type="button" data-workspace="Chapter">▤ <span>Chapter</span></button><button class="selected" type="button" data-workspace="Checkpoints">▱ <span>Checkpoints</span></button><button type="button" data-workspace="Media">▧ <span>Media</span></button><button type="button" data-workspace="Sources">❝ <span>Sources</span></button><button type="button" data-workspace="Rights">♧ <span>Rights</span></button><button type="button" data-workspace="Releases">▣ <span>Releases</span></button>
      </div>
      <button class="collapse-nav" type="button" data-collapse-nav>« <span>Collapse sidebar</span></button>
    </nav>

    <section class="chapter-canvas" aria-label="Structured chapter editor">
      <p class="editor-status" data-editor-status aria-live="polite">Checking editor session…</p>
      <article class="chapter-prose" data-prose>
        <h1>7.3 &nbsp; Eudaimonia and the AI-Assisted Life</h1>
        <p>For Aristotle, <em>eudaimonia</em> is not a feeling but an activity of soul in accordance with virtue over a complete life. It is neither fleeting pleasure nor momentary success, but a stable disposition to choose, act, and perceive well.</p>
        <p>AI systems can support many human activities, yet they do not, by themselves, constitute a good life. They are tools, environments, and interlocutors, not ends. The question is not whether AI can make us happy, but whether and how its use can be integrated into a life oriented by practical wisdom.</p>
        <p class="passage selected-passage" tabindex="0" data-passage-id="ch07-p0041"><button class="passage-marker" type="button" aria-label="Add a checkpoint anchored to this passage" data-anchor>▱<span class="visually-hidden">Add checkpoint</span><small>1</small></button>Character is formed through repeated actions chosen for their own sake (NE II.1). If we routinely rely on AI to deliberate, remember, or judge, we risk cultivating habits of dependence that erode the virtues of practical reason. Conversely, if we use AI with discernment—recognizing its limits, correcting its errors, and refusing its vices—we may strengthen our own capacities.</p>
        <h2>7.4 &nbsp; Friends, Communities, and Digital Participation</h2>
        <p>Aristotle emphasizes that we become just by acting justly with others (NE II.1). The AI-mediated spaces in which we speak, learn, and decide together are now central to our moral formation. These spaces can cultivate friendship and cooperation, or corrode them through manipulation, anonymity, and scale.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="media-toolbar" role="group" aria-label="Insert media"><button type="button" class="add-media" data-media-menu aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="media-insert-choices" aria-label="Show or hide media choices">+</button><div class="media-menu" id="media-insert-choices" data-media-options><button type="button" data-media="Image or GIF">▧ Image or GIF</button><button type="button" data-media="YouTube">▹ YouTube</button><button type="button" data-media="Vimeo">∨ Vimeo</button><button type="button" data-media="X post">𝕏 X post</button><button type="button" data-media="Spotify">♫ Spotify</button><button type="button" data-media="SoundCloud">◒ SoundCloud</button><button type="button" data-media="Bluesky">☁ Bluesky</button><button type="button" data-media="Audio/Video">♬ Audio/Video</button><button type="button" data-media="PDF">□ PDF</button><button type="button" data-media="Link card">↗ Link card</button></div></div>
      <div class="text-block-editor" data-text-editor hidden><label>Selected text block<textarea data-text-value></textarea></label><button type="button" data-save-text>Save text change</button></div>
      <p class="snapshot-receipt" data-snapshot-receipt hidden></p>
      <section class="human-release-review" data-human-review hidden aria-labelledby="human-review-title">
        <div class="human-review-heading"><div><p class="review-eyebrow">Submitted snapshot</p><h2 id="human-review-title">Human release review</h2></div><strong data-review-state>Awaiting decision</strong></div>
        <dl class="snapshot-identity"><div><dt>Immutable snapshot hash</dt><dd><code data-snapshot-hash>—</code></dd></div><div><dt>Snapshot revision</dt><dd><code data-snapshot-revision>—</code></dd></div></dl>
        <p class="release-warning" id="release-review-warning"><strong>Approval does not publish.</strong> It records a human release decision for this exact immutable snapshot. Final promotion remains GitHub-gated.</p>
        <label>Optional approval note<textarea data-approval-comment maxlength="2000" aria-describedby="release-review-warning"></textarea></label>
        <button class="approve-release" type="button" data-approve-release aria-describedby="release-review-warning">Approve release snapshot</button>
        <details class="reject-review"><summary>Reject this snapshot</summary><label>Reason for rejection<textarea data-rejection-comment maxlength="2000" required aria-describedby="release-review-warning"></textarea></label><button type="button" data-reject-release aria-describedby="release-review-warning">Reject snapshot</button></details>
        <p class="decision-status" data-decision-status aria-live="polite"></p>
      </section>
    </section>

    <aside class="checkpoint-inspector" data-inspector aria-label="Prompt checkpoint inspector">
      <div class="inspector-heading"><h2>Prompt checkpoint</h2><button type="button" data-inspector-close aria-label="Close checkpoint inspector">×</button></div>
      <p class="offline-note" data-offline-note hidden>Read-only/offline: changes remain in this browser and cannot be published.</p>
      <div class="checkpoint-tabs" data-checkpoint-tabs aria-label="Chapter checkpoints"></div>
      <label>Type<select data-checkpoint-type disabled><option selected>Commit</option><option>Work</option><option>Reconcile</option></select></label>
      <div class="field-pair"><label>Stage<input data-checkpoint-stage /></label><label>Strategy<select data-checkpoint-strategy><option>initial-judgment</option><option>self-explanation</option><option>argument-reconstruction</option><option>evidence-warrant</option><option>contrast-case</option><option>counterexample</option><option>consider-alternative</option><option>objection-repair</option><option>question-generation</option><option>epistemic-calibration</option><option>framework-comparison</option><option>transfer</option><option>metacognitive-trace</option></select></label></div>
      <label>Title<input data-checkpoint-title /></label><label>Trigger<textarea class="short-textarea" data-checkpoint-trigger></textarea></label>
      <label>Prompt<textarea data-prompt>Evaluate the claim that delegating deliberation to AI systems can be consistent with the formation of virtue. Use Aristotle's account of habituation (NE II.1) and discuss at least one concrete example.</textarea></label>
      <label>Guidance<textarea class="short-textarea" data-checkpoint-guidance></textarea></label>
      <label>Passage anchor<select data-anchor-select><option>7.3 &nbsp; Eudaimonia and the AI-Assisted Life</option></select></label>
      <p class="anchor-note">Anchors to selected passage. <button type="button" data-edit-anchor>Edit anchor</button></p>
      <label class="toggle-row">Show in sidebar preview <input type="checkbox" checked data-sidebar-preview /><span aria-hidden="true"></span></label><p class="field-help">Students will see this checkpoint in the sidebar.</p>
      <label>Student response format<select data-response-format><option value="prose" selected>Prose</option><option value="movement-plus-prose">Movement plus prose</option></select></label>
      <div class="word-limits"><label>Min. words<input data-min-words type="number" min="1" max="1000" value="250" /></label><label>Max. words<input data-max-words type="number" min="1" max="1000" value="750" /></label></div>
      <label>Rationale<textarea class="short-textarea" data-checkpoint-rationale></textarea></label>
      <button class="inspection-row" type="button" data-a11y>Accessibility check <span class="good">✓ No issues detected</span> ›</button>
      <label>Editorial approval<select><option selected>● Needs review</option><option>✓ Approved</option></select></label>
      <button class="add-checkpoint" type="button" data-add-checkpoint>+ Add checkpoint</button><button class="save-checkpoint" type="button" data-save-checkpoint hidden>▱ Save checkpoint</button><button class="remove-checkpoint" type="button" data-remove-checkpoint hidden>Remove checkpoint</button>
      <p class="checkpoint-count" data-checkpoint-count>0 draft checkpoints of 3. Add Commit first; the order is immutable.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <section class="agent-activity" data-agent-drawer aria-label="Semantic review">
    <div class="agent-tabs"><button type="button" data-agent-toggle aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="semantic-review-summary">✧ <strong>Review changes</strong><span aria-hidden="true">⌃</span></button><span>Semantic changes <b data-semantic-count>0</b></span><span>Working version <strong data-working-version>—</strong></span></div>
    <div class="agent-diff semantic-review" id="semantic-review-summary" data-review-summary tabindex="-1"><p class="accepted-message">Loading the canonical comparison…</p></div>
  </section>
</main>

<dialog class="media-inspector" data-media-dialog aria-labelledby="media-dialog-title">
  <form method="dialog" data-media-form><div class="inspector-heading"><h2 id="media-dialog-title" data-media-title>Insert media</h2><button type="button" data-media-close aria-label="Close media inspector">×</button></div>
  <label data-media-ref-label>Canonical URL<input type="url" inputmode="url" autocomplete="url" data-media-url required placeholder="https://" /></label><label>Title<input type="text" data-media-title-input required /></label>
  <div class="native-upload" data-native-upload hidden><label class="advanced-toggle"><input type="checkbox" data-existing-asset /> Use existing reviewed asset IDs <span>Advanced option for agent-prepared media</span></label><label data-file-field>Native media file<input type="file" data-media-file /></label><p class="gif-note" data-gif-note hidden>GIF remains animated media. Placement defaults to click-to-play with a static poster in print.</p><div class="review-controls" data-review-controls><fieldset><legend>Rights declaration</legend><label>Rights basis<select data-rights-basis required><option value="owned">Owned</option><option value="licensed">Licensed</option><option value="permission">Permission</option><option value="publicDomain">Public domain</option><option value="fairUse">Fair use</option><option value="unknown">Unknown — needs review</option></select></label><label>Creator or rights holder<input type="text" data-rights-creator required /></label><label>Source URL <span>Optional; public HTTPS only</span><input type="url" inputmode="url" data-rights-source placeholder="https://" /></label><label>License or terms <span>Optional</span><input type="text" data-rights-license /></label><label>Required attribution<textarea data-rights-attribution required></textarea></label></fieldset><fieldset><legend>Editorial declaration</legend><label>Teaching use<textarea data-review-teaching-use required></textarea></label><label>Placement intent<textarea data-placement-intent required></textarea></label></fieldset><fieldset><legend>Accessibility declaration</legend><label class="review-ack"><input type="checkbox" data-decorative /> This asset is decorative and needs no alt text.</label><label data-review-alt-field>Reviewed alt text<textarea data-review-alt required></textarea></label><label>Motion review<select data-motion-review><option value="notApplicable">Not applicable</option><option value="pending">Pending</option><option value="passed">Passed</option><option value="failed">Failed</option></select></label><div data-transcript-declaration hidden><label>Transcript/equivalent language<input type="text" data-caption-language value="en" /></label><label>Substantive transcript/equivalent<textarea data-review-transcript></textarea></label></div></fieldset><label data-poster-alt-field hidden>Reviewed video poster alt text<textarea data-poster-alt></textarea></label><button class="create-review-package" type="button" data-create-review-package>Create pending review package</button><section class="review-package-receipt" data-review-package-receipt hidden aria-label="Pending media review package"><div><strong data-review-package-state>Pending human decision</strong><code data-review-package-hash></code></div><p data-review-package-summary></p><p><strong>Pending is not clearance.</strong> Upload may proceed, but release remains blocked until a human clears this exact declaration hash.</p><label>Required decision comment<textarea data-review-decision-comment maxlength="2000"></textarea></label><div class="review-decision-actions"><button type="button" data-clear-review-package>Clear exact package</button><button type="button" data-block-review-package>Block exact package</button></div></section><p class="upload-progress" data-review-package-status aria-live="polite"></p></div><p class="review-required-note">The editor first creates a server-issued <strong>pending</strong> review package from these declarations. Uploads remain <strong>reviewRequired</strong>; package creation and placement do not clear or approve the media.</p><label class="review-ack"><input type="checkbox" data-review-ack /> I understand that package creation, upload, and placement are not rights, editorial, accessibility, or release approval.</label><p class="upload-progress" data-upload-progress aria-live="polite"></p></div>
  <div class="existing-asset-fields" data-existing-fields hidden><div class="media-library"><div class="media-library-search"><label>Search reusable media<input type="search" data-media-search maxlength="100" placeholder="Title or exact SHA-256" /></label><label>Kind<select data-media-kind><option value="">Any kind</option><option value="image">Image</option><option value="audio">Audio</option><option value="video">Video</option><option value="document">Document</option></select></label><label>Rights<select data-media-rights><option value="cleared">Cleared</option><option value="reviewRequired">Review required</option><option value="blocked">Blocked</option><option value="">Any state</option></select></label><button type="button" data-media-search-submit>Search library</button></div><p class="field-help">Choose a persisted asset to pin its exact latest version and rights case. Only cleared media can enter a release snapshot.</p><div class="media-library-results" data-media-results aria-live="polite"></div></div><details class="raw-media-ids"><summary>Enter exact IDs manually <span>Advanced recovery</span></summary><label data-media-id-field>Media ID<input type="text" data-media-id placeholder="media_…" /></label><label data-media-version-field>Media version ID<input type="text" data-media-version-id placeholder="mediaVersion_…" /></label><label data-rights-case-field>Rights case ID<input type="text" data-rights-case-id placeholder="rights_…" /></label></details></div>
  <label data-caption-field>Caption<textarea data-media-caption required placeholder="State what the media shows and why it appears here."></textarea></label><label data-alt-field>Alt text<textarea data-media-alt required placeholder="Convey the essential visual information, without repeating the caption."></textarea></label><label data-transcript-field hidden>Transcript declaration or location<textarea data-media-transcript></textarea></label><label>Teaching use / credit<input type="text" data-media-credit required /></label><label data-fallback-field hidden>Authored fallback summary<textarea data-x-fallback placeholder="Describe this resource for readers who do not activate the live embed."></textarea></label><label data-link-label-field hidden>Link label<input type="text" data-link-label maxlength="120" placeholder="Open resource" /></label><p class="provider-privacy" data-provider-privacy hidden></p><p class="field-help" data-media-help>Raw embed HTML is never accepted.</p><button class="save-checkpoint" type="submit" data-media-submit>Add to change set</button></form>
</dialog>

<script>
  type Block = { type: string; blockId?: string; text?: string; code?: string; level?: number; passageId?: string; items?: string[]; ordered?: boolean; rows?: string[][]; language?: string; title?: string; caption?: string; alt?: string; canonicalUrl?: string; figureId?: string; embedId?: string; linkId?: string };
  type Checkpoint = { checkpointId?: string; passageId: string; passageExcerptHash: string; slot: "commit" | "work" | "reconcile"; stage: string; strategy: string; title: string; trigger: string; prompt: string; guidance: string; responseStructure: "prose" | "movement-plus-prose"; minWords: number; maxWords: number; rationale: string; showInSidebar: boolean };
  type Chapter = { title?: string; body?: Block[]; checkpoints?: Checkpoint[] };
  const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-editor-root]")!;
  if (!root) throw new Error("Editor root missing");
  const gatewayOrigin = root.dataset.contentApiOrigin?.replace(/\/$/, "") ?? "";
  const status = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-editor-status]")!;
  const chapterPicker = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-chapter]")!;
  const offline = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-offline-note]")!;
  const inspector = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-inspector]")!;
  const prose = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-prose]")!;
  const login = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-login]")!;
  const logout = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-logout]")!;
  const addCheckpoint = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-add-checkpoint]")!;
  const saveCheckpoint = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-save-checkpoint]")!;
  const removeCheckpoint = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-remove-checkpoint]")!;
  const textEditor = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-text-editor]")!;
  const textValue = root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-text-value]")!;
  const snapshotReceipt = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-snapshot-receipt]")!;
  const humanReview = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-human-review]")!;
  const snapshotHashValue = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-snapshot-hash]")!;
  const snapshotRevisionValue = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-snapshot-revision]")!;
  const reviewState = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-review-state]")!;
  const approvalComment = root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-approval-comment]")!;
  const rejectionComment = root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-rejection-comment]")!;
  const approveRelease = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-approve-release]")!;
  const rejectRelease = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-reject-release]")!;
  const decisionStatus = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-decision-status]")!;
  const submitReview = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-submit-review]")!;
  const checkpointTabs = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-checkpoint-tabs]")!;
  const checkpointCount = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-checkpoint-count]")!;
  const checkpointType = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-checkpoint-type]")!;
  const stage = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-checkpoint-stage]")!;
  const strategy = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-checkpoint-strategy]")!;
  const checkpointTitle = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-checkpoint-title]")!;
  const trigger = root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-checkpoint-trigger]")!;
  const prompt = root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-prompt]")!;
  const guidance = root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-checkpoint-guidance]")!;
  const anchor = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-anchor-select]")!;
  const sidebarPreview = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-sidebar-preview]")!;
  const responseStructure = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-response-format]")!;
  const minWords = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-min-words]")!;
  const maxWords = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-max-words]")!;
  const rationale = root.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-checkpoint-rationale]")!;
  const mediaDialog = document.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>("[data-media-dialog]")!;
  const mediaTitle = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-media-title]")!;
  const mediaRefField = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-media-ref-label]")!;
  const nativeUpload = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-native-upload]")!;
  const existingAsset = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-existing-asset]")!;
  const existingFields = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-existing-fields]")!;
  const mediaSearch = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-media-search]")!;
  const mediaKind = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-media-kind]")!;
  const mediaRights = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-media-rights]")!;
  const mediaSearchSubmit = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-media-search-submit]")!;
  const mediaResults = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-media-results]")!;
  const fileField = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-file-field]")!;
  const mediaFile = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-media-file]")!;
  const reviewControls = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-review-controls]")!;
  const reviewPackageStatus = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-review-package-status]")!;
  const createReviewPackage = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-create-review-package]")!;
  const reviewPackageReceipt = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-review-package-receipt]")!;
  const reviewPackageState = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-review-package-state]")!;
  const reviewPackageHash = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-review-package-hash]")!;
  const reviewPackageSummary = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-review-package-summary]")!;
  const reviewDecisionComment = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-review-decision-comment]")!;
  const clearReviewPackage = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-clear-review-package]")!;
  const blockReviewPackage = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-block-review-package]")!;
  const rightsBasis = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-rights-basis]")!;
  const rightsCreator = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-rights-creator]")!;
  const rightsSource = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-rights-source]")!;
  const rightsLicense = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-rights-license]")!;
  const rightsAttribution = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-rights-attribution]")!;
  const reviewTeachingUse = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-review-teaching-use]")!;
  const placementIntent = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-placement-intent]")!;
  const decorative = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-decorative]")!;
  const reviewAltField = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-review-alt-field]")!;
  const reviewAlt = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-review-alt]")!;
  const motionReview = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>("[data-motion-review]")!;
  const transcriptDeclaration = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-transcript-declaration]")!;
  const captionLanguage = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-caption-language]")!;
  const reviewTranscript = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-review-transcript]")!;
  const posterAltField = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-poster-alt-field]")!;
  const posterAlt = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-poster-alt]")!;
  const gifNote = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-gif-note]")!;
  const reviewAck = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-review-ack]")!;
  const uploadProgress = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-upload-progress]")!;
  const mediaRef = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-media-url]")!;
  const mediaName = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-media-title-input]")!;
  const mediaCaption = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-media-caption]")!;
  const mediaAlt = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-media-alt]")!;
  const mediaCredit = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-media-credit]")!;
  const mediaId = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-media-id]")!;
  const mediaVersionId = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-media-version-id]")!;
  const rightsCaseId = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("[data-rights-case-id]")!;
  const mediaIdField = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-media-id-field]")!;
  const mediaVersionField = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-media-version-field]")!;
  const rightsCaseField = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-rights-case-field]")!;
  const mediaTranscript = mediaDialog.querySelector<HTMLTextAreaElement>("[data-media-transcript]")!;
